  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the most critical first step is to establish the simplest possible baseline to anchor all future comparisons. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the most minimal configuration in the space: a single RNA profile encoded with PCA (a fast, interpretable linear method). This tells us (1) whether RNA data alone carries sufficient signal for the task, (2) the performance floor against which more complex encoders (scvi, scgpt), multiprofile aggregation, and multimodal fusion must be judged, and (3) whether the task is solvable from a single modality at all. Establishing this floor first ensures that subsequent experiments—testing image-only, multimodal, or more sophisticated encoders—can be interpreted against a known reference rather than in a vacuum. Under a 10-experiment budget, spending one slot on the simplest baseline is the highest-information-per-experiment choice before exploring the richer design space."
}

